# Docker & Infra

```bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose up --build
```

## Serviços

| Nome | Build / imagem | Porta |
|------|----------------|-------|
| `postgres` | `postgres:16-alpine` | 5432 |
| `api` | `nexus-backend/Dockerfile` | 3000 |
| `frontend` | `nexus-frontend/Dockerfile` (nginx) | 5173 |

Versões mais recentes compatíveis; backend: `node:24-alpine` (ver `engines`).

## Startup

1. `postgres` — `pg_isready`
2. `api` — `db migrate` (migrations em `migrations/app/`) → seed → `node dist/main.js`
3. `frontend` — após `GET /api/v1/health`

Build da API inclui `npm run contract:emit`. Migrations versionadas commitadas em `nexus-backend/migrations/app/`.

## Entrypoint API (referência)

```bash
npx prisma db migrate
npx tsx src/prisma/seed.ts
node dist/main.js
```

Primeira bootstrap local (antes de existir migration): `migration plan --name initial` → commit → `db migrate`.

## Variáveis (`.env.example`)

```env
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://commandix:commandix@postgres:5432/commandix
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=change-me-access
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=change-me-refresh
JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES_IN=15m
JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRES_IN=7d
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api/v1
HTTP_TRIGGER_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
```

`VITE_API_URL` é build-time.

